    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6928" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναλογ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>based on mathematical ratios,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1144f
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>in Nic.</u>
				p.100P.
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κὴ τέχνη</span> the art <i>of
				applying analogy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				1.199
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ -κοί</span>”
				<i>the analogical school of grammarians,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Suid.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτρείδης</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				802.38
			</span></i>.</div>
